 "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JeSt9VqfdhoQfbbGVpm6gn", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53713, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JeSt9VqfdhoQfbbGVpm6gn", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55036, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01J6LKPWwcrT6mdpDrYC1P3c", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55336, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J6LKPWwcrT6mdpDrYC1P3c", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55336, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J6LKPWwcrT6mdpDrYC1P3c", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60164, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Bad release:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy (v2.3.1-rc also failed health checks).\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished in all three regions. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the SEV2 timed out, but the incident list showed it had already been created, so I didn't send it again. Only one page went out. The incident summary describes the failure, the rollback (including the halt partway through), the current state and two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error.\n\nThe first follow-up is a prerequisite for redeploying v2.3.1. Neither version has ever been healthy, so redeploying either one also needs approval from the change manager.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SkdqQ76czhfwguW7RVcdSS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VxFkCpjNfKy3jLDnoEoMNh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest healthy release is v2.3.0. Rolling back.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012UY3YBycqSPtGR2ewGjXmK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Bgq6raqLmUKPGVQQawDE7W", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back before the orchestrator stopped. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I'm retrying once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Q3X2wFyTC6zDfdYWHSs5No", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018un6dUaEUKv2Q27uGofKp9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EqSbXkq4vNkZpntkf2CPSN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JeSt9VqfdhoQfbbGVpm6gn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of v2.3.1, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. A retry finished the rollback in us-west and eu-west. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) and investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J6LKPWwcrT6mdpDrYC1P3c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Bad release:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy (v2.3.1-rc also failed health checks).\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished in all three regions. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the SEV2 timed out, but the incident list showed it had already been created, so I didn't send it again. Only one page went out. The incident summary describes the failure, the rollback (including the halt partway through), the current state and two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error.\n\nThe first follow-up is a prerequisite for redeploying v2.3.1. Neither version has ever been healthy, so redeploying either one also needs approval from the change manager.", "type": "text"}]}]}